# pool-swap-notice-surface: task pool-event-context-leak (2026-10-14) — the operator swap
# notice must surface via ctx.ui.notify (L3) and NEVER as a pi.sendMessage custom message.
# Pre-fix behavior (contract §10 F30 false claim): every successful pool auto-swap sent a
# customType:"swarm-pool-event" custom message (display:true, deliverAs:"followUp"); pi
# persists and LLM-converts EVERY custom message (role:custom → role:user), so each swap
# leaked a "⚠ Pool: …" line into the agent's context permanently. Post-fix: the agent
# consumes ONLY the continue-note (customType:"swarm-message"), the operator sees the swap
# warning as a TUI notification, and the session carries no pool-event line at all.
#
# Pattern 2 (seeded world): the lane's swarm.yml defines a 2-slot pool. Slot A is the fixture
# model (pool-swap-notice-surface, quota-strike burst); slot B (pool-swap-notice-b fixture) is
# HEALTHY so the gate exhausts into a NORMAL (non-probe) swap A→B, whose recovery turn runs on
# the B fixture and completes.
